93#issuecomment-3729764988","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114693","id":3729764988,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eT7J8","user":{"login":"Faulpilz","id":243077102,"node_id":"U_kgDODn0P7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243077102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz","html_url":"https://github.com/Faulpilz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T16:47:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T16:47:38Z","body":"[first-game.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24531691/first-game.zip)\n\nSorry, it was not the .godot dir, but the .exe I created and forgot to delete, that bloated the zip.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3729764988/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730708166","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114693#issuecomment-3730708166","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114693","id":3730708166,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eXhbG","user":{"login":"Faulpilz","id":243077102,"node_id":"U_kgDODn0P7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243077102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz","html_url":"https://github.com/Faulpilz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T21:59:42Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T21:59:42Z","body":"After a little bit more testing, I propably can reproduce the issue. It seems like it only occurs to labels nested in a pure Node. Any label directly under the Node2D parent or for example under a CharacterBody2D stays visible after reopening the project. Just the children beneath the \"Node\" nodes I used as GameManager and folders become invisible everytime.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730708166/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3732314466","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114693#issuecomment-3732314466","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114693","id":3732314466,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7edpli","user":{"login":"Faulpilz","id":243077102,"node_id":"U_kgDODn0P7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243077102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz","html_url":"https://github.com/Faulpilz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-10T09:53:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-10T09:53:41Z","body":"Another addition:\nThe issue is the order of rendering. In the editor the labels were printed beneath the TileMap. Turning the TileMap invisible showed all labels, making it visible again hid them. Seems like the editor renders the graphical nodes in another order than the runtime, otherwise I do not understand, why all labels are visible at runtime from the start on. Adding or deleting a single Labels seems to rerender all of them, therefore, after a duplication, all of them were now displayed above the TileMap again. I fixed the problem by giving all labels an ordering of z=1, which should be done in generell here, I guess. Still, it seems like the discrepancy between render ordering of editor and runtime could be considered a minor bug.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3732314466/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3734273373","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114693#issuecomment-3734273373","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114693","id":3734273373,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7elH1d","user":{"login":"Faulpilz","id":243077102,"node_id":"U_kgDODn0P7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243077102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz","html_url":"https://github.com/Faulpilz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faulpilz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-11T09:04:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-11T09:05:42Z","body":"Same issue now with TileMapLayer Nodes.\n\nNode2D\n|_ Node\n...|_ TileMapLayer (Background)\n...|_ TileMapLayer2 (Mid)\n\nWhen opening the project, mid is not visible in the editor because it is rendered under background but at runtime everything is rendered as expected. Reordering both nodes (dragging mid above background and then back beneth in the tree) turns everything to normal. Editing mid by adding a tile did not change anything. Duplicating worked as with labels.\n\nWill contribute a newer version of the project:\n\n[first-game2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24549278/first-game2.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3734273373/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5078064337","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114693#issuecomment-5078064337","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114693","id":5078064337,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLq0c0Q","user":{"login":"ELginas","id":42967362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyOTY3MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42967362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas","html_url":"https://github.com/ELginas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-25T10:00:01Z","updated_at":"2026-07-25T10:00:01Z","body":"I don't think Control, Node2D, Node3D or any nodes inheriting them (e.g. TileMapLayer) are intended to be a child of Node. Node2D or Control should be used instead of Node. Parenting Control, Node2D or Node3D to a Node would cause issues with positioning and transformation as Node doesn't store any transformation data. So it is best to use same parent node type as the child, e.g. Control parent for Control nodes, Node2D for Node2D nodes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5078064337/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]